# `tex` with `d|p` writes the elements of d as well as p, so the
# address through %r1 after it is not 4 * %tid.x + param_0 but unknown,
# and the store it guards runs on at most the CTA's 32 threads. `tex` is
# not classified, so its work is in no total.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/texture_outputs.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	tex.1d.v4.s32.s32 	{%r1, %r2, %r3, %r4}|%p1, [micro_texture_outputs_tex, {%r1}]; // not classified (its FLOPs and bytes not counted){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p1 st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r2; // <= warp * × lane * | exec <= 32/CTA | global store addr ? (value defined by unsupported instruction `tex`){{$}}
